    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Choice C — Teaching Tips (Typography Challenge)\r\n\r\n- **Keep changes focused and incremental.**  \r\n  Encourage students to improve one typography area at a time (headings, then body text, then emphasis elements) and preview between changes.\r\n\r\n- **Require a quick plan before prompting.**  \r\n  If students ask for “better typography,” push them to name a specific issue (e.g., weak hierarchy, hard-to-read body text) and what must remain consistent.\r\n\r\n- **Watch for readability trade-offs.**  \r\n  Common issues include overly large headings, cramped line spacing, long line lengths, or decorative fonts that reduce clarity. Encourage students to briefly resize the preview to confirm the text remains readable on smaller screens.\r\n\r\n- **Connect changes to user experience.**  \r\n  Ask: “Does this make the content easier to scan and read?” Require a short version comment explaining what changed and why it improves clarity.",
